# Umbra environment — copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This repo reads `.env`, not `.env.local`. Both are gitignored (`.env*`); this
# file is the one exception, kept committed by the `!.env.example` negation.
#
# TWO KINDS OF VARIABLE, AND THE PREFIX IS THE DIFFERENCE:
#
#   VITE_*  is compiled into the browser bundle. Anyone who loads the site can
#           read it. Only put a key here if it is dev-only or origin-restricted.
#   no prefix  is server-only — read by the Vercel functions in `api/`, never by
#           the browser. Set these in the Vercel dashboard, not in a local `.env`
#           (there is no serverless runtime in `npm run dev`).
#
# Adding a `VITE_` prefix to a server-only key is exactly what put the Foursquare
# key in the bundle (#218/#219). Don't.
#
# QUOTING: values in this repo are written quoted, and the readers strip one
# surrounding pair (`normalizeApiKey`, `foursquareApiKey`). A quoted key that
# reaches a `Bearer` header upstream comes back 401 and reads as an expired key,
# so if you add a new reader, strip the quotes there too.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client (browser bundle)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Required. Basemap tiles. https://cloud.maptiler.com — restrict it to your
# origins in the dashboard, because it does ship in the bundle.
VITE_MAPTILER_API_KEY=""

# Public Cloudflare Worker origin only—never an R2 credential or bucket key.
# Production value: https://shademap-nyc-shadow-staging.marcoctpolo.workers.dev
# The app reads only its small /_shadow/current.json pointer; it does not fetch
# manifest or tile payloads unless the separate debug transport below is enabled.
VITE_SHADOW_API_BASE=""

# Debug only. Exactly "true" enables the isolated v2 tile transport and visual
# overlay. Leave unset in Vercel Production; it does not affect live shadows or routes.
VITE_SHADOW_V2_DEBUG=""

# Public origin serving the published NYC transit dataset (pointer, manifest,
# shards) — never an R2 credential or bucket key. Absent, transit routing
# falls back to Overpass and no transit request is made.
# Public value: https://pub-c960c9abbd204246901a291a24850f55.r2.dev
VITE_TRANSIT_BASE=""

# Public origin serving the published NYC navigation dataset (pointer,
# manifest, street/building shards) — never an R2 credential or bucket key.
# Absent, the static dataset stays off, existing Overpass paths answer, and no
# navigation-data request is made. Leave empty in production until Checkpoint 6
# rollout; the intended value is the delivery Worker below.
# Intended: https://shademap-nyc-shadow-staging.marcoctpolo.workers.dev
VITE_NAVIGATION_BASE=""

# Dev only. Place popups. In production `api/fsq.js` injects `FSQ_API_KEY`
# server-side and the browser sends no Foursquare credential at all — the
# `import.meta.env.DEV` guard in `app/services/foursquare.ts` folds this away in
# a production build. Foursquare service keys carry no origin restriction, which
# is why the key must not reach the bundle. https://foursquare.com/developers
VITE_FOURSQUARE_API_KEY=""

# Dev only. Umbra Assistant LLM: Google Gemini free tier, called through the Vite
# `/__gemini` proxy. Free key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# One shared pool: comma-separate several keys here, and/or use the numbered
# vars; requests round-robin and fail over on 429/5xx/401/403. In production
# `api/agent.js` holds `GEMINI_API_KEY` instead.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=""
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY_1=""
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY_2=""
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY_3=""

# Optional. Per-role models — the loop researches with one and writes with the
# other; if they resolve to the same model it skips the separate write call.
# Defaults: research `gemini-3.5-flash-lite`, response `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`;
# VITE_GEMINI_MODEL overrides both.
VITE_GEMINI_RESEARCH_MODEL=""
VITE_GEMINI_RESPONSE_MODEL=""
VITE_GEMINI_MODEL=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only (Vercel project settings — never prefixed with VITE_)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# FSQ_API_KEY=            # api/fsq.js — the production Foursquare key
# GEMINI_API_KEY=         # api/agent.js — comma-separated pool, or GEMINI_API_KEY_1..9

# Optional knobs, all with defaults in the proxies themselves:
# FSQ_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=            # extra origins beyond the deployment's own
# FSQ_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=
# AGENT_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
# AGENT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=
# AGENT_MAX_PAYLOAD_BYTES=
# GEMINI_ALLOWED_MODELS=          # added to the built-in allowlist
# NOMINATIM_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_MS=
# NOMINATIM_CACHE_SECONDS=
# OVERPASS_ENDPOINTS=             # comma-separated ordered endpoint URLs
# OVERPASS_MAX_BODY_BYTES=
